 "Radius": "",
 "Feeding the networks": "",
 "Each network is added in the terminal: sudo zenithboard menu → 1 ADSB. Their own installers ask questions as they go (a station name, an e-mail, a sharing key) and give a claim link or code to keep: the console runs commands that ask nothing, and keeps no key.": "",
 "Its page ↗": "",
 "terminal": "",
 "ADSB Exchange comes first and is always on; FlightAware, Flightradar24 and Plane Finder only if you want them. Their state is also on the overview.": "",
 "What to collect": "",
 "All of it stays on the card; nothing is sent anywhere.": "",
 "A sample every 15 minutes, 30 days kept: the /stats page and the summaries' figures.": "",
 "Years of the decoder's graphs on port 8542; its author's installer, a few minutes.": "",
 "Registrations and models read on the card (tar1090).": "",
 "Needs the receiver map (tar1090), not seen on this Pi.": "",
 "What keeps it running": "",
 "Recommended for a Pi left alone. Each one off again puts back what it found.": "",
 "The chip restarts a frozen Pi after about 10 seconds.": "",
 "No router for 6 minutes: the network restarts; 12: the Pi.": "",
 "Up to 50 MB, to read what happened before a freeze.": "",
 "Debian's security channel only; feeders untouched, no reboot.": "",
 "Retry without end after a loss; no radio power saving.": "",
 "Sharing on Bluesky": "",
 "Account @{account}. Posting each crossing is switched in Sharing; the summaries here.": "",
 "No Bluesky account on this Pi: it is set up in the terminal (it asks for an app password): sudo zenithboard social setup. Skip this step until then.": "",
 "Summary of the last 24 hours": "",
 "Every day at its time (21:00 unless changed in Sharing), from the statistics.": "",
 "Summary of the week": "",
 "Sunday 19:00 unless changed; four posts, two minutes apart.": "",
 "They need the statistics: switch them on in step 5.": "",
 "Your phone, and this computer": "",
 "Scan a QR code once and the phone stays signed in, no password typed, as long as it opens the console once a month. Face ID and passkeys need HTTPS under a domain name, which a Pi at a home address does not have.": "",
 "Pair a phone now": "",
 "Sign computers in with the phone": "",
 "A computer's sign-in page then shows a QR code; the phone says yes, no password.": "",
 "Ready": "",
 "Nothing to change": "",
 "Applied one after the other; each is the zenithboard command you can read in Activity.": "",
